ing filenames \(e.g., `Stage_v4_final_edit.vwx`\),)Tj T* 1.187378 Tw (creating severe version divergence. While high-end visualizers like Unreal Engine)Tj T* 2.735244 Tw (and Disguise D3 offer photorealistic real-time rendering, their steep hardware)Tj T* 2.38935 Tw (prerequisites and specialized operational complexity make them impractical for)Tj T* 0 Tw (general multi-departmental production coordination [6].)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 38 417.4 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 1.887422 Tw 9.1 TL/F2 7.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 28.8 Tm (Furthermore, these standalone desktop suites enforce rigid licensing models that)Tj T* 1.187378 Tw (restrict access to dedicated technical workstation operators, effectively walling off)Tj T* 1.069156 Tw (non-technical stakeholders such as event coordinators, artistic directors, and venue)Tj T* 0 Tw (facility managers who are essential to the approval loop.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 38 404.6 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 9.8 TL/F6 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 1.6 Tm (B. Web-Based 3D Graphics and Collaborative Virtual Environments)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 38 312.4 cm 0 0 0 rg BT .029782 Tw 9.1 TL/F2 7.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 83.4 Tm (The evolution of WebGL and WebGPU standards has enabled complex 3D viewports)Tj T* .488545 Tw (directly inside standard web browsers without third-party plugins [3]. Cabiddu et al.)Tj T* .1996 Tw ([3] surveyed web-based collaborative 3D environments, identifying browser memory)Tj T* 3.0032 Tw (constraints and DOM-to-canvas event synchronization as primary architectural)Tj T* .588727 Tw (challenges. The emergence of React Three Fiber \(R3F\) [9] established a declarative)Tj T* 1.219527 Tw (component model for Three.js, binding the imperative 3D scene graph to reactive)Tj T* 1.19995 Tw (component lifecycles. While platforms like Figma revolutionized 2D collaborative)Tj T* 2.2022 Tw (design, translating real-time multi-user synchronization to 3D spatial coordinate)Tj T* 1.75665 Tw (spaces with heterogeneous departmental constraints remains an open engineering)Tj T* 0 Tw (frontier.)Tj T*