 Tw (client-server architecture integrating React, TypeScript, Three.js, and React Three)Tj T* 2.428275 Tw (Fiber with Supabase managed cloud infrastructure. To guarantee concurrent)Tj T* 4.661657 Tw (operational integrity without update thrashing, StageSync implements an)Tj T* 4.349025 Tw (Optimistic Concurrency Control \(OCC\) protocol paired with a granular)Tj T* 1.0526 Tw (Role-Based Access Control \(RBAC\) engine that maps departmental privileges to)Tj T* 1.589775 Tw (3D scene-graph mutations. Furthermore, we formalize a venue-aware artificial)Tj T* 1.236825 Tw (intelligence pipeline capable of performing monocular depth estimation, ground)Tj T* 2.5638 Tw (plane segmentation, metric camera pose calibration, and constrained spatial)Tj T* 2.206133 Tw (optimization to synthesize editable 3D parametric stage layouts directly from)Tj T* 4.046571 Tw (uploaded venue photographs and user-specified boundary dimensions. We)Tj T* 2.002971 Tw (formulate an empirical verification framework evaluating system performance,)Tj T* 6.3798 Tw (collaborative throughput, and state synchronization latency. StageSync)Tj T* 1.5615 Tw (demonstrates a scalable, frictionless paradigm for modern computational event)Tj T* 0 Tw (engineering.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 38 325.5 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 1.1083 Tw 9.4 TL/F6 7.8 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 20.4 Tm (Index Terms)Tj/F3 7.8 Tf <97436f6c6c61626f726174697665207669727475616c20656e7669726f6e6d656e74732c20636f6d70757465722067726170686963732c206576656e74>Tj T* 1.9364 Tw (production engineering, optimistic concurrency control, spatial computing,)Tj T* 0 Tw (Three.js, venue-aware AI stage generation.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 38 310.2 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 10.8 TL/F3 8.9 Tf 1 0 0 1 90.94395 1.9 Tm (I. INTRODUCTION)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 38 244.5 cm 0 0 0 rg BT .56535 Tw 9.1 TL/F2 7.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 56.1 Tm (Live event production is an intrinsically collaborative, multidisciplinary engineering)Tj T* 1.299689 Tw (discipline operating under rigid, unyielding temporal constraints [1]. Mounting an)Tj T* 4.7588 Tw (arena-scale concert, theatrical performance, or global corporate conference)Tj T* .17395 Tw (necessitates the synchronized convergence of multiple specialized departments: stage)Tj T* 6.258171 Tw (carpenters, structural riggers, lighting designers, audio engineers, video)Tj T* 1.421289 Tw (projectionists, props masters, and creative art directors. Each department operates)Tj T* 0 Tw (with distinct spatial objectives, safety tolerances, and technical vocabularies.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 38 231.7 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 9.8 TL/F6 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 1.6 Tm (A. Background and Industrial Landscape)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 38 148.6 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 1.121418 Tw 9.1 TL/F2 7.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 74.3 Tm (Historically, spatial planning in live event production has relied on heavy desktop)Tj T* .1711 Tw (Computer-Aided Design \(CAD\) packages such as Vectorworks Spotlight, AutoCAD,)Tj T* 2.6502 Tw (or specialized visualizers like CAST WYSIWYG [2]. While these tools offer)Tj T* .622444 Tw (millimetric drafting precision, they were engineered for isolated single-user desktop)Tj T* .826343 Tw (workstations. Concurrently, operational production timelines, task assignments, and)Tj T* 2.16608 Tw (cue sheets are managed in disconnected cloud spreadsheets, email threads, and)Tj T* .295782 Tw (messaging apps. Consequently, a modification in stage riser dimensions made by the)Tj T* .9944 Tw (carpentry crew often fails to propagate to lighting riggers or sound engineers until)Tj T* 0 Tw (equipment has physically arrived on the arena floor.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 38 92 cm 0 0 0 rg BT .87712 Tw 9.1 TL/F2 7.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 47 Tm (Furthermore, the live event industry is characterized by compressed on-site load-in)Tj T* .165891 Tw (schedules, where touring crews frequently have fewer than twelve hours to transform)Tj T* 1.0468 Tw (an empty arena into a fully operational concert environment. Under such stringent)Tj T* 1.371467 Tw (operational pressure, any unresolved spatial ambiguity directly translates into idle)Tj T* 2.876267 Tw (crew labor, emergency re-rigging, delayed sound checks, and potential safety)Tj T* 0 Tw (infractions.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 38 79.2 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 9.8 TL/F6 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 1.6 Tm (B. Problem Statement and Workflow Fragmentation)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 38 41.6 cm 0 0 0 rg BT .551511 Tw 9.1 TL/F2 7.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 28.8 Tm (This technological fragmentation induces four major vulnerabilities across the event)Tj T* .68636 Tw (lifecycle: \(1\) )Tj/F4 7.6 Tf (Spatial Clashing and Occlusion:)Tj/F2 7.6 Tf ( Stage props, line-array speakers, and)Tj T* 2.67625 Tw (lighting trusses are frequently positioned in competing volumetric coordinates,)Tj T* 7.3428 Tw (necessitating hasty, unsafe on-site rigging workarounds. \(2\) )Tj/F4 7.6 Tf (Revision)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 313 555.4 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 1.513333 Tw 9.1 TL/F4 7.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 47 Tm (Desynchronization:)Tj/F2 7.6 Tf ( Disparate teams work on out-of-date revisions of floor plans,)Tj T* 3.992667 Tw (causing compounding communication breakdowns. \(3\) )Tj/F4 7.6 Tf (Asymmetric Technical)Tj T* 2.65345 Tw (Literacy:)Tj/F2 7.6 Tf ( Non-technical stakeholders, clients, and creative directors struggle to)Tj T* 1.06712 Tw (interpret complex 2D technical schematics, leading to delayed approvals. \(4\) )Tj/F4 7.6 Tf (High)Tj T* 1.7692 Tw (Cold-Start Latency:)Tj/F2 7.6 Tf ( Designing initial stage layouts from raw venue photography)Tj T* 0 Tw (requires hours of manual drafting before creative planning can even begin.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 313 489.7 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 1.6734 Tw 9.1 TL/F2 7.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 56.1 Tm (In conventional pre-production pipelines, cross-departmental reconciliation occurs)Tj T* 1.352873 Tw (through ad-hoc markup of static PDF technical riders. When the lighting director)Tj T* 2.081091 Tw (repositions an overhead truss to avoid beam occlusion, this change is typically)Tj T* -.042367 Tw (communicated via email or chat messages. Because the audio lead and props manager)Tj T* 1.506767 Tw (lack access to a centralized dynamic spatial scene, they remain unaware that the)Tj T* .641236 Tw (modified truss clamps obstruct the main stage left line-array sightline until physical)Tj T* 0 Tw (truss elevation begins on site.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 313 442.2 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 2.023745 Tw 9.1 TL/F2 7.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 37.9 Tm (This lack of unified spatial visibility also severely hinders client and executive)Tj T* 3.2512 Tw (sign-off. Executive producers and external event clients often evaluate stage)Tj T* .57844 Tw (feasibility solely from 2D top-down schematics, only to express dissatisfaction with)Tj T* 2.54304 Tw (sightline blockages or aesthetic stage dressing once physical assembly is well)Tj T* 0 Tw (underway, leading to expensive emergency modifications.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 313 429.4 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 9.8 TL/F6 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 1.6 Tm (C. Proposed Solution: The StageSync Framework)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 313 364.5 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 2.2404 Tw 9.1 TL/F2 7.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 56.1 Tm (To address these critical shortcomings, we introduce )Tj/F3 7.6 Tf (StageSync)Tj/F2 7.6 Tf (, an end-to-end)Tj T* 3.8913 Tw (cloud-native 3D stage planning and production management ecosystem. By)Tj T* 2.0076 Tw (leveraging client-side WebGL/WebGPU rendering within modern web browsers,)Tj T* 1.943543 Tw (StageSync eliminates native client software installations, enabling cross-platform)Tj T* 3.3612 Tw (accessibility on mobile tablets, laptops, and workstations. StageSync couples)Tj T* 3.875029 Tw (interactive 3D spatial authoring with real-time transactional synchronization,)Tj T* 0 Tw (multi-role access governance, and automated AI spatial reconstruction.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 313 335.2 cm 0 0 0 rg BT .3959 Tw 9.1 TL/F2 7.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 19.7 Tm (StageSync establishes a single source of spatial truth where every 3D asset mutation)Tj T* 3.36688 Tw (instantly reflects across all connected client viewports, bound to a rigorous)Tj T* 0 Tw (departmental approval and milestone governance state machine.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 313 322.4 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 9.8 TL/F6 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 1.6 Tm (D. Research Objectives and Key Contributions)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 313 312.1 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 9.1 TL/F2 7.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 1.5 Tm (The primary contributions of this paper are summarized as follows:)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 313 282.8 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 9.1 TL/F2 7.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 19.7 Tm <7f20>Tj/F3 7.6 Tf (Architectural Formulation:)Tj/F2 7.6 Tf ( We formulate a multi-tier collaborative web)Tj T* 8 0 Td (architecture synthesizing React, TypeScript, Three.js, and Supabase into a unified,)Tj T* (low-latency 3D stage production management environment [3].)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 313 244.8 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 9.1 TL/F2 7.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 28.8 Tm <7f20>Tj/F3 7.6 Tf (Multi-Role Concurrency & Governance:)Tj/F2 7.6 Tf ( We design an Optimistic Concurrency)Tj T* 8 0 Td (Control \(OCC\) synchronization protocol paired with an explicit eight-role)Tj T* (departmental RBAC security matrix and an Art Director review-approval state)Tj T* (machine.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 313 215.9 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 9.1 TL/F2 7.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 19.7 Tm <7f20>Tj/F3 7.6 Tf (Photometric & Acoustic Spatial Simulation:)Tj/F2 7.6 Tf ( We incorporate physical simulation)Tj T* 8 0 Td (equations directly into the 3D scene graph, enabling real-time photometric lux)Tj T* (verification and ISO 9613-2 acoustic sound pressure distribution modeling.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 313 177.9 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 9.1 TL/F2 7.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 28.8 Tm <7f20>Tj/F3 7.6 Tf (Venue-Aware AI Spatial Synthesis:)Tj/F2 7.6 Tf ( We formalize a five-stage deep learning)Tj T* 8 0 Td (pipeline combining monocular depth estimation, ground plane segmentation, and)Tj T* (energy-minimization spatial optimization to convert 2D venue photographs into)Tj T* (editable 3D parametric stage blockouts [4], [5].)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 313 149 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 9.1 TL/F2 7.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 19.7 Tm <7f20>Tj/F3 7.6 Tf (Empirical Verification Framework:)Tj/F2 7.6 Tf ( We establish a comprehensive evaluation)Tj T* 8 0 Td (methodology and benchmark matrix to quantify collaborative throughput, state)Tj T* (synchronization latency, and spatial conflict elimination.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 313 120.1 cm 0 0 0 rg BT .123055 Tw 9.1 TL/F2 7.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 19.7 Tm (By democratizing 3D spatial planning across all production tiers through an intuitive,)Tj T* 3.499933 Tw (cloud-synchronized browser environment, StageSync eliminates the traditional)Tj T* 0 Tw (barriers between technical drafters and creative decision-makers.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 313 54.4 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 1.029867 Tw 9.1 TL/F2 7.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 56.1 Tm (The subsequent sections of this paper are organized as follows: Section II surveys)Tj T* 1.46688 Tw (related work in desktop CAD, collaborative virtual environments, and spatial AI.)Tj T* 1.362 Tw (Section III details the proposed system architecture, rendering pipeline, and OCC)Tj T* 2.638133 Tw (protocol. Section IV articulates core functional modules, RBAC matrices, and)Tj T* .49712 Tw (physics simulation engines. Section V presents the venue-aware AI stage generation)Tj T* 1.676311 Tw (pipeline. Section VI outlines the empirical evaluation framework and discussion,)Tj T* 0 Tw (followed by concluding remarks in Section VII.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 1 1 rg 1 1 1 RG 140 665 335 14 re B Q q 0 0 0 rg 0 0 0 RG BT/cour 7 Tf 1 0 0 1 226.2 670.5 Tm[(abhishek.r.2024.csd@rajalakshmi.edu.in)]TJ ET Q q 0 0 0 rg 0 0 0 RG BT/cour 7 Tf 1 0 0 1 230.4 660.5 Tm[(harini.m.2024.csd@rajalakshmi.edu.in)]TJ ET Q /Fm1 Do q 1 1 1 rg 1 1 1 RG 232.5 648.281 147.00034 8.742981 re B Q q Q

